  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Back at the restaurant, the staff is waiting to see if Max will finally return to work after everything that happened. They discuss his possible arrival. Let us listen to their conversation in Russian first.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Тебя это тоже волнует?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Что именно?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Например, Макс придёт или нет?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Я думаю, он придёт.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Он любит нашу кухню.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "И он любит работать.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "А как же шеф?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Шеф его простит.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Они помирятся.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Конечно помирятся.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Тогда всё будет хорошо.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Да, просто ждём.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let us examine the conversation line by line.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Тебя это тоже волнует?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Does this worry you too?' Here 'you' sets up the idea, while 'to worry' comes at the end for emphasis.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Что именно?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'What exactly?' You'll hear 'what' all the time in the show, here connected with 'what'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Например, Макс придёт или нет?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'For example, will Max come or not?' Here 'for example' sets up the idea, while 'will come' comes at the end for emphasis. Senya answers straight away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Я думаю, он придёт.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I think he will come.' Senya starts with 'I' and pairs it with 'I think' to make the point clear.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Он любит нашу кухню.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'He loves our kitchen.' Ilya puts 'he' up front so the listener immediately catches the tone, followed by 'loves'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "И он любит работать.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And he loves to work.' The key word here means 'he', which Senya combines with 'loves'. Then Ilya replies.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "А как же шеф?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And what about the chef?' Ilya puts 'how' up front so the listener immediately catches the tone, followed by 'chef'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Шеф его простит.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'The chef will forgive him.' — Notice the proper name meaning 'chef, boss' paired with the pronoun for 'him'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Они помирятся.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'They will make peace.' The first content word means 'they', and 'to make up' rounds out the thought. And Senya jumps in.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Конечно помирятся.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Of course they will make peace.' A compact expression built around 'of course' and 'to make up'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Тогда всё будет хорошо.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Then everything will be fine.' The first content word means 'back then', and 'good' rounds out the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Да, просто ждём.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Yes, we are just waiting.' A compact expression built around 'just' and 'we wait'. Now let us listen to the conversation once again.",
      "gap": 0.9
